    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a clear mandate: prioritize speed and favorable matchups to exploit vulnerable arms. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (81.25) stands as our premier play of the day. While his position in the 8-hole tempers his run-scoring upside, the combination of a high-ceiling matchup against Fedde and a slow delivery-profile from the opposing battery creates an ideal runway for a stolen base, which remains our primary focus in this 5x5 format. He is joined in the top tier by **Christian Yelich** (71.68), who benefits from a favorable platoon split against Ober and a similar SB-readiness profile. Both players are positioned to carry our offensive efficiency, provided they capitalize on these situational edges.\n\nConversely, we are exercising extreme caution with our heavy hitters facing elite arms. **Trea Turner** (48.87) and **Kyle Schwarber** (47.62) are both relegated to \"marginal\" status as they stare down Skenes. Despite the pedigree of both players, the sheer dominance of the opposing arm creates a high risk of stagnant output, forcing us to lean on the higher-efficiency profiles of **Hyeseong Kim** (61.65) and **Junior Caminero** (63.35) to anchor the lineup. **Chase Meidroth** was our most difficult bench decision, narrowly missing the cut with a score of 49.85; he was ultimately pushed out by the superior platoon leverage offered by **Carson Benge** against the soft xERA of Rodr\u00edguez, E.\n\nManagers should monitor the wind reports, specifically regarding **Colt Keith** (53.97), whose marginal score is further dragged down by an unfavorable inward breeze. While **Luke Raley** (57.95) and **Yordan Alvarez** (58.90) remain technically start-worthy, they sit near the lower bounds of our \"Strong\" tier due to park factors and the quality of their respective opposing starters. We are currently holding **Caleb Durbin** and **Kazuma Okamoto** in reserve due to lack of lineup confirmation, and we will look to re-integrate them into tomorrow's rotation should they return to action with better environmental conditions.",
